---
import FeaturedLessons from '../components/FeaturedLessons.astro';
import LearningRoutes from '../components/LearningRoutes.astro';
import BookLayout from '../layouts/BookLayout.astro';

import { chapters } from '../data/chapters.js';
import { withBasePath, withPagePath } from '../utils/paths.js';
---

<BookLayout title="Home" lang="en">
  <div style="text-align: right; color: var(--secondary-color); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Last update: 2026-11-25</div>
  <h1>Foundation Model Engineering</h1>
  <p><strong>Learn how foundation models work—and what breaks when you train, serve, and evaluate them.</strong> A free, open-source textbook in English and Korean, with interactive explanations, PyTorch examples, and CPU labs.</p>
  <p>Start with one engineering question below, follow a learning route, or use the full table of contents. You will need basic Python, linear algebra, and probability; the <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-1/learning-path-and-mastery')}>prerequisite check</a> helps you find gaps.</p>

  <p><strong>November 24 model update:</strong> explore <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-17/commercial-model-benchmarks')}>43 model profiles</a>, including <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-17/commercial-model-benchmarks') + '#model-glm-54'}>GLM-5.4</a>, GPT-6.2 Astra/Sol and Gemini 4 Neon/Carbon. Check release status, compare evaluation settings, and run a long-context cost example. The <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-11/audio-and-speech-integration')}>speech</a>, <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-11/image-diffusion-models')}>image</a> and <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-11/commercial-video-models')}>video/world-model</a> chapters cover their separate evaluation questions.</p>

  <FeaturedLessons lang="en" />
  <LearningRoutes lang="en" />

  <h2>Build something you can test</h2>
  <p>The <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-7/tiny-decoder-lab')}>tiny decoder lab</a> runs on a CPU. Train a causal model, remove its access to earlier tokens, and test whether a resumed run follows the same trajectory. The <a href={withPagePath('/chapter-17/experimental-design-and-uncertainty')}>evaluation lab</a> asks a different question: is a measured improvement strong enough to justify a release?</p>
  <p>Start the decoder experiment: <a href="https://colab.research.google.com/github/sungeuns/foundation-model-engineering/blob/main/public/labs/tiny-decoder-lab.ipynb">open the notebook in Colab</a> or <a href={withBasePath('/labs/tiny-decoder-lab.ipynb')}>download it for Jupyter</a>. It uses CPU PyTorch and generates its own data. No model download or API key is needed; Colab execution requires Google sign-in.</p>
  <p>The {chapters.reduce((total, chapter) => total + chapter.subs.length, 0)} lessons connect architectures, training, inference, retrieval, agents, evaluation, and safety. Short quizzes ask you to explain a failure or choose a trade-off. Illustrative calculations and authored simulations are labeled; they are not measurements of a production model.</p>

  <h2>Help make the book better</h2>
  <p>This is an independent project by Seongeun So, developed with AI assistance. Sources and limitations belong next to the claims they support. If an explanation, translation, or experiment does not hold up, <a href="https://github.com/sungeuns/foundation-model-engineering/issues">open an issue</a> with the page and a counterexample.</p>
  <p>If a lesson helped you, share that lesson with someone working on the same problem. <a href="https://github.com/sungeuns/foundation-model-engineering">Star the repository</a> to bookmark it, or <a href="https://github.com/sungeuns/foundation-model-engineering/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md">contribute a correction</a>.</p>

  <h2>Table of Contents</h2>
  <div class="toc">
    {chapters.map(ch => (
      <div class="toc-chapter">
        <h3>{ch.title.en}</h3>
        <ul>
          {ch.subs.map(sub => (
            <li><a href={withPagePath(sub.path)}>{sub.title.en}</a></li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

</BookLayout>

<style>
  .toc {
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }
  .toc-chapter {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  .toc h3 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: #111;
  }
  .toc ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding-left: 1rem;
  }
  .toc li {
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }
  .toc a {
    text-decoration: none;
    color: var(--accent-color);
  }
  .toc a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
